{
  "abstract": "The first machine-checked proof of Feige's conjecture in its GENERAL-δ form (previous Lean work, LeanPool's Feige/, covers only δ = 1). The mathematics follows Ling's proof (arXiv:2608.18392); the formalization also proves two steps the paper leaves unproved (Claim 3.4 and the minimisation over m in Corollary 1.3). Lean 4 proofs of (1) Feige's conjecture in its general form: for independent, nonnegative, integrable X₁, …, Xₙ with E[Xᵢ] ≤ μ (μ > 0) and every δ > 0, P(∑ Xᵢ − E[∑ Xᵢ] < δμ) ≥ min(δ/(1+δ), e⁻¹); and (2) the lower-bound half of Samuels' conjecture (Ling's Theorem 1.1): for ordered means 0 ≤ m₁ ≤ … ≤ mₙ, λ > ∑ mᵢ and independent nonnegative Xᵢ with E[Xᵢ] = mᵢ, P(∑ Xᵢ < λ) ≥ minᵢ ∏_{j ≥ i} (1 − mⱼ/(λ − ∑_{k<i} mₖ)). The proofs follow Z. Ling, On Samuels' Conjecture (arXiv:2608.18392): a two-point mixture decomposition (vendored from LeanPool), Bernoullification and a Bellman-type induction on weighted Bernoulli sums. The sharpness and attainment half of Ling's Theorem 1.1 is not formalized.",
